content.text:
I would not merge this branch or trust the “9/9 wins” conclusion yet. The review found five blocking P1 issues and three P2 regressions.

::code-comment{title="[P1] Remove benchmark-specific answers from product code" body="This recognizes a benchmark task and hard-codes both the answer (`retrievalDefaultLimit = 5`) and exact validation test. Equivalent answer generators exist for XDG at line 3062 and Codex schema at line 3096, while the harness tells agents to apply decisive actions and stop. The candidate binary therefore contains an answer key that main does not, so the reported improvement measures task memorization rather than general Brain quality." file="/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/internal/cli/agent_surface.go" start=2999 end=3013 priority=1 confidence=0.99}

::code-comment{title="[P1] Keep the query benchmark comparable with main" body="The task now requires a branch-only constant and exposes the exact target value in validation. origin/main still has two literal defaults of 10, so this setup replacement cannot run there. Because hide_expected_from_agent and hide_validation_from_agent are also absent, prompt_for gives the agent both the target file and `retrievalDefaultLimit = 5`. This is neither the same task across refs nor a blind agent scenario." file="/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/tasks/entire-brain-query-default-limit.json" start=8 end=21 priority=1 confidence=0.99}

::code-comment{title="[P1] Do not promote retrieved prose into decisive edits" body="All retrieved docs and history are copied into History.Matches. The downstream Historical assignments parser trusts a marker in that prose, associates assignments with any likely file containing the same name, chooses a lexical test, and can mark it complete_on_pass. A stale or malicious document can therefore manufacture an exact edit instruction. Assignments need structured provenance tied to the original file and revision, and unverified prose must never produce a decisive action." file="/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/internal/cli/retrieve_cmd.go" start=186 end=193 priority=1 confidence=0.98}

::code-comment{title="[P1] Stop treating limit comparisons as broken assignments" body="The substring check for `= limit` also matches comparisons such as `>= limit`, and it treats normal internal assignments as unnormalized caller input. Running the current HEAD's brief on the clean default-limit task produced 16 bogus normalizeLimit actions, mostly against retrieve.go and agent_surface.go, despite the requested default already being correct. Parse assignment structure rather than matching substrings, and emit nothing without evidence that the value is untrusted." file="/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/internal/cli/agent_surface.go" start=3471 end=3475 priority=1 confidence=0.99}

::code-comment{title="[P1] Enforce actual Brain use for every Brain condition" body="The audit requires a Brain call only for tasks with require_local_brain_search. semantic_brain and ordinary full_brain rows can ignore the prescribed Brain command and still have audit.ok=true; used_brain merely changes a few soft score points. Consequently a successful no-Brain agent can be counted as a valid branch datapoint, contrary to the requirement to verify tool use from every session log." file="/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py" start=1799 end=1823 priority=1 confidence=0.99}

::code-comment{title="[P2] Do not classify every slash as a file path" body="Natural-language queries containing a slash skip token fallback entirely. On current HEAD, `refresh status freshness` returns 10 symbols while `refresh/status freshness` returns zero. Only classify a query as a path when the whole value has path-like structure; slashed concepts, URLs, and prose should retain semantic fallback." file="/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/internal/cli/semantic.go" start=3809 end=3818 priority=2 confidence=0.99}

::code-comment{title="[P2] Keep indexed retrieval off the live source tree" body="Every search/query of at least eight characters invokes a repository scan that reads up to 2,500 source files of up to 512 KiB each; likely-file generation can perform another scan. That turns an indexed lookup into potentially more than a gigabyte of synchronous source I/O and silently ignores files after the cap. Move live-code hints behind brief or a dedicated option and derive ordinary retrieval solely from indexed data." file="/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/internal/cli/retrieve_cmd.go" start=231 end=242 priority=2 confidence=0.97}

::code-comment{title="[P2] Avoid reseeding every sessionless repository refresh" body="seedNeededForBrain returns true whenever the manifest has no sessions, before checking whether the existing seed matches HEAD or the worktree fingerprint. Default MCP brain_refresh intentionally skips sessions, so a repository without checkpoint history is reseeded and its docs rebuilt on every call. Seed freshness must be independent of session availability." file="/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/internal/cli/refresh.go" start=699 end=708 priority=2 confidence=0.96}

Verification completed:

- `go test ./...` passed.
- `go vet ./...` passed.
- All 249 Python harness tests passed.
- Worktree remains clean.

The green tests do not invalidate these findings: several tests explicitly assert the benchmark-specific answers and “do not search broader” behavior, so they preserve the overfitting rather than detect it.

